#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""opencloddie - run Claude Code in a tmux session shipped to your server.

Install:
  curl -fsSL https://your.opencloddie.host/install/opencloddie \
    -o ~/.local/bin/opencloddie && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/opencloddie

First run configures the server URL and API key, creates a tmux session running
Claude Code pointed at the opencloddie gateway, starts a small agent that ships
each terminal channel to the web UI, and attaches your terminal.

  opencloddie                 new/reuse a session in the current directory
  opencloddie --name work     named session
  opencloddie ls              list sessions
  opencloddie attach work     re-attach locally
  opencloddie stop work       stop the tmux session and unregister it
  opencloddie web             open the web UI
  opencloddie env             print gateway environment variables
  opencloddie exec [...]      run claude in this terminal via the gateway

Ctrl-b d detaches the local terminal; the tmux session and its agent keep
running, so the web UI can still drive it.
"""

